From aabb8ea29874c5aaa6cb7c774b08f0f8dac0a1ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: facetimehd downstream <facetimehd-downstream@localhost>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 11/21] v4l2: fix buffer ownership between vb2, the driver and
 the firmware

The descriptor tag the firmware echoes back was a kernel pointer to the
buffer context, so a confused firmware could make the driver
dereference anything. Use a generation counter instead and look the
context up by tag. Protect buffer state with a spinlock shared with the
return handler, and reject malformed buffer returns, failing the queue
after repeated protocol errors.

Return every driver-owned buffer to vb2 on every path: when channel
start fails part-way, when a send fails, and at STREAMOFF, which no
longer waits without a timeout on firmware that may never answer.
Refuse S_FMT while buffers exist, check the buffer size in
buf_prepare(), and propagate v4l2_ctrl_handler_setup() errors.
